# P2P API testing

## 1. Oracle

`docs/API.md` and `/openapi.json` say what is right. When the API disagrees, the test keeps the documented expectation and fails — never change the expectation to match the API; report it. What neither document says is in `docs/QUESTIONS.md` as assumed: don't assert it until a human answers.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — API.md rule 1: vnd-002 → 400 inactive_vendor_gate
const res = await request.post('/purchase-orders', {
  data: { vendor_id: 'vnd-002', line_items: [{ sku: 'LUM-2X4-8', quantity: 1, unit_price: 4.75 }] },
});
expect(res.status()).toBe(400);
expect((await res.json()).rule).toBe('inactive_vendor_gate');

// ❌ BAD — API returned 201, so the test was “fixed” to pass
expect([201, 400]).toContain(res.status());
```

## 2. Black box

Never read or change `src/`. Tests exercise the API over HTTP only.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const res = await request.get('/purchase-orders/po-does-not-exist');

// ❌ BAD
import { purchaseOrders } from '../../src/store';
```

## 3. Requests

Use Playwright's `request` fixture with paths only; the host comes from `baseURL`. Never a hard-coded URL.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
await request.get('/vendors');
await request.post('/invoices', { data: { po_id, invoice_number, line_items } });

// ❌ BAD
await request.get('http://localhost:8000/vendors');
```

## 4. Data

Every test creates what it needs — its own vendor when it checks exposure, unique invoice numbers with `Date.now()`. Never call `POST /admin/reset` in a test. Never depend on another test's data, except inside one serial flow.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const create = await request.post('/vendors', { data: { name: `Exposure QA ${Date.now()}` } });
const invoiceNumber = `INV-${Date.now()}`;

// ❌ BAD
await request.post('/admin/reset');
await request.get('/vendors/vnd-001/exposure'); // assumes prior test approved an invoice for vnd-001
```

## 5. Per endpoint

For each endpoint: **positive** (it works), **negative** (one invalid input, one change at a time → 400 `validation_error` or the business rule), **errors** (unknown id → 404).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — GET /vendors/{vendorId}/exposure: 200 after approve flow, vnd-002 inactive N/A for exposure math, vnd-missing → 404
test('EXP-GET-E01 unknown vendor returns 404', { tag: '@api' }, async ({ request }) => {
  expect((await request.get('/vendors/vnd-no-such/exposure')).status()).toBe(404);
});

// ❌ BAD — only GET /health 200; no POST /vendors empty name, no GET exposure 404
```

## 6. Assertions

Assert the status; for every 400, the exact `rule`; the values that matter, not only that a field exists; the shape, with `expectSchema` (P48). A 400 with the wrong rule is a failed test.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const receive = await request.post(`/purchase-orders/${poId}/receive`, {
  data: { items: [{ sku: 'LUM-2X4-8', quantity: 999 }] },
});
expect(receive.status()).toBe(400);
expect((await receive.json()).rule).toBe('receive_quantity_limit');

const exposure = await request.get(`/vendors/${vendorId}/exposure`);
expect(exposure.status()).toBe(200);
const body = await exposure.json();
expect(body.open_ap_liability).toBe(95.1);
await expectSchema(request, body, 'VendorExposure');

// ❌ BAD
expect((await receive.json()).rule).toBe('workflow_gate'); // docs say receive_quantity_limit
expect(body).toHaveProperty('open_ap_liability');
```

## 7. Tags

Exactly one tag per test: `{ tag: '@api' }` for one endpoint, `{ tag: '@e2e' }` for a flow. On `test()`, never on `describe()`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
test('INV-POST-02 duplicate invoice number returns 400', { tag: '@api' }, async ({ request }) => { ... });
test('P2P happy path draft to exposure', { tag: '@e2e' }, async ({ request }) => { ... });

// ❌ BAD
test.describe('invoices', { tag: '@api' }, () => { ... });
```

## 8. Known bugs

A test for a confirmed bug keeps its assertions and gets `test.fail(true, 'BUG-<n>: <one line>')` — never deleted, never loosened.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — docs: duplicate_invoice_detection (INV-7 = inv-7)
test('INV-POST duplicate invoice case-insensitive', { tag: '@api' }, async ({ request }) => {
  test.fail(true, 'BUG-3: second inv-7 accepted with 201');
  expect(second.status()).toBe(400);
  expect((await second.json()).rule).toBe('duplicate_invoice_detection');
});

// ❌ BAD — bug masked in the test
expect(second.status()).toBe(201);
```

## 9. Evidence

Label every claim **executed**, **inspected only**, or **not yet tested** (comments, reports, `docs/QUESTIONS.md`).

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
- POST /purchase-orders/{poId}/submit on draft → submitted — executed
- Decimal quantities on PO lines — assumed until answered (docs/QUESTIONS.md §4) — inspected only
- Match failure status/body — not yet tested

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
- All workflow_gate paths covered (no label)
```
